def make(i,prompt,opts,ans,exp,strat,steps,diff): return {"id":f"question-english-performance-1-iv-4-{i}","subject":"english","type":"single-choice","prompt":prompt,"options":[{"id":k,"text":v} for k,v in opts.items()],"knowledgeIds":[KG],"difficulty":diff,"answer":{"value":ans,"explanation":exp},"provenance":{"origin":"original","license":"All rights reserved","sourceUrl":SOURCES[0]["url"],"sourceLocator":"三份公開英文試題僅供能力方向研究；未複製原題、選項、文章或答案。","authoringNote":"依官方課綱 KG 與公開英文試題的日常溝通理解能力方向獨立編寫；待第二輪 AI／Terra 內容複核。"},"reviewStatus":"draft","updatedAt":"2026-09-09","lessonId":LESSON,"examPatternRefs":refs(),"solutionStrategy":strat,"solutionSteps":steps}
Q=[
make(1,"A: Are you free after school? B: I have basketball practice until five. A: How about five thirty? What is the main purpose of the exchange?",{"A":"To arrange a meeting time","B":"To report a lost book","C":"To order food","D":"To describe a sport rule"},"A","A asks about availability, B gives a practice time, and A suggests five thirty; together they are arranging when to meet.","Track each speaker's proposal and time expression, then summarize the action they are trying to complete.",["Identify A's question about being free.","Note B's practice ends at five.","Notice A proposes five thirty.","Connect the times with arranging a meeting.","Choose A because the exchange negotiates a meeting time."],"easy"),
make(2,"A: Did you see my blue umbrella? B: It was next to the music room after lunch. A: I'll check there. Where will A probably go next?",{"A":"The music room","B":"The cafeteria kitchen","C":"The bus office","D":"The sports field"},"A","B gives the last known location as next to the music room, so A will probably check that place.","Use the final location clue and the speaker's stated plan to infer the next action.",["Find what A is looking for: a blue umbrella.","Locate B's evidence: it was next to the music room.","Read A's response: I'll check there.","Match there with the previously named place.","Select A and ignore locations not mentioned in the dialogue."],"easy"),
make(3,"A: Would you like tea or juice? B: Juice, please. A: With ice? B: Yes, thank you. What is happening?",{"A":"Someone is choosing a drink","B":"Someone is borrowing a bicycle","C":"Someone is booking a room","D":"Someone is asking for directions"},"A","The choices tea or juice and the question about ice show that the speakers are preparing a drink order.","Collect the concrete nouns and follow-up question to identify the activity rather than focusing on one isolated sentence.",["List the choices: tea and juice.","Notice the follow-up about ice.","Connect both clues with ordering or choosing a drink.","Reject bicycle, room, and directions because no matching clues appear.","Choose A and summarize the exchange as a drink choice."],"easy"),
make(4,"A: The library closes at six today. B: Then we should return the books before dinner. Why does B say this?",{"A":"Because the library will not be open later","B":"Because dinner is served in the library","C":"Because the books are new gifts","D":"Because B wants to play outside"},"A","B connects returning the books with the library's closing time, so the reason is that it will not be open later.","Link the time information in A to the action proposed by B.",["Find the key fact: the library closes at six.","Find B's planned action: return the books before dinner.","Ask why the action must happen before then.","Match the closing time with the library not being open later.","Choose A because it explains the timing directly."],"medium"),
make(5,"A: Your presentation starts in ten minutes. B: I still need to print the last page. A: I can help you at the office. What does A offer?",{"A":"Help B print the page","B":"Cancel the presentation","C":"Borrow B's notebook","D":"Explain the office rules"},"A","A says I can help and identifies the office, so A offers assistance with printing the last page.","Use the problem stated by B and match it with the concrete help offered by A.",["Identify B's problem: the last page is not printed.","Notice the time pressure of ten minutes.","Read A's offer: I can help you at the office.","Connect help with the unfinished printing task.","Select A because it states the proposed assistance."],"medium"),
make(6,"A: How was the school play? B: The actors were excellent, but the microphones were too quiet. What is B's overall opinion?",{"A":"The play was good, with a sound problem","B":"The play was canceled before it began","C":"The actors were absent","D":"The microphones were the best part"},"A","Excellent actors show a positive feature, while quiet microphones show a problem; B gives a mixed but mainly positive evaluation.","Combine both sides of a but sentence instead of reporting only the first or second clause.",["Record the positive detail: the actors were excellent.","Record the problem after but: the microphones were too quiet.","Combine the two details into one balanced summary.","Reject cancellation, absent actors, and praise of microphones.","Choose A because it includes both the strength and the problem."],"medium"),
make(7,"A: Can you feed my cat this weekend? B: I can, but I need the key on Friday. What condition does B mention?",{"A":"B needs the key before the weekend","B":"B cannot visit until next month","C":"The cat needs a new home","D":"The key is inside the cat's bowl"},"A","B agrees to feed the cat but says the key is needed on Friday, so the key must be provided before the weekend visit.","Separate the agreement from the condition introduced by but and need.",["Identify the requested task: feed the cat this weekend.","Notice B agrees with I can.","Find the condition: B needs the key on Friday.","Place Friday before the weekend in the timeline.","Select A because it states the required preparation."],"medium"),
make(8,"A: The weather report says heavy rain tonight. B: Let's move the picnic to Sunday. What decision do they make?",{"A":"They change the picnic day","B":"They cancel school for a month","C":"They buy a new tent tonight","D":"They move the picnic indoors immediately"},"A","Because heavy rain is expected, B proposes moving the picnic to Sunday; the decision changes its day.","Use the weather as the reason and the proposed new day as the outcome.",["Identify the problem: heavy rain tonight.","Find the suggested action: move the picnic.","Find the destination in time: Sunday.","Distinguish changing a day from canceling or changing location.","Choose A because it states the decision supported by the dialogue."],"medium"),
make(9,"A: I cannot find the homework file. B: Check the shared class folder; I uploaded it there this morning. Where should A look?",{"A":"The shared class folder","B":"The school gate","C":"The art supply cabinet","D":"The cafeteria menu"},"A","B explicitly directs A to the shared class folder and says the file was uploaded there.","Give priority to the direct location instruction and use the time phrase only as supporting evidence.",["Identify the missing item: the homework file.","Read B's command: Check the shared class folder.","Use uploaded it there to confirm the location.","Remove the unrelated school locations.","Select A and restate the next action as checking that folder."],"easy"),
make(10,"A: Are you joining the volunteer cleanup? B: Yes. I will bring gloves and arrive at eight. What will B do?",{"A":"Join the cleanup and bring gloves at eight","B":"Stay home and call at noon","C":"Sell gloves after school","D":"Arrive without joining the activity"},"A","B says yes to joining, names gloves, and gives an arrival time of eight; A combines all three details.","Integrate the answer, object, and time instead of selecting an option that keeps only one clue.",["Record B's direct answer: Yes.","Record the object B will bring: gloves.","Record the arrival time: eight.","Check which option includes participation, object, and time together.","Choose A because it preserves every relevant detail."],"hard"),
]
